  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56c941340668-0000-0008"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked: \"Is it perfectly workable to say that if the defendant has been taken to the police station, they can't then search the car?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56c941340668-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked: \"Are you more concerned about the ability to search the vehicle or the protection of the officer?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56c941340668-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked: \"You've arrested this guy for reckless driving. He was going 25 miles over the speed limit, okay? And you're going to search his car for evidence? Of what?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56c941340668-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer questioned whether the search was contemporaneous with the arrest, noting that \u201cif it isn\u2019t contemporaneous, that\u2019s a new world.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56c941340668-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked: \"What does contemporaneous have to do with officer safety? It has to do with timing, doesn\u2019t it?\""
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56c941340668-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer later asked whether the stare decisis doctrine should apply if an earlier decision was wrong."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. YANG",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56c941340668-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. YANG, mr. Yang testified that \u201cthe protection of the officer is what motivates the doctrine.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. YANG",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "56c9413406686c6e6878d5e43998876326775631be129d5a1ee201bcaf96f4bd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-56c941340668-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. YANG, mr. Yang explained that when a suspect is under custodial arrest, there is an increased incentive to escape, obtain weapons, and destroy incriminating evidence."
      }
    ],
